invariant: INV-46
file: mlkem.c
catches: test/mlkem-builds.sh
reason: mlkem.c guards its call to the vector NTT on a macro no build
  defines, so a host object's sessions run mlkem_poly.c's forward
  loops. Nothing else objects: mlkem_vector.c still compiles and links,
  bin/mlkem_vector_equiv_test calls it directly, and every vector
  passes, because the loops compute the same coefficients; only the time
  is wrong. Every session of a host object runs the vector NTT, so the
  script compiles mlkem.c as a host object does and requires it to call
  mlk_vector_ntt and not mlk_poly_ntt.

--- old
#ifdef CH_CPU_RUNTIME
    mlk_vector_ntt(p);
--- new
#ifdef CH_CPU_RUNTIME_PATH
    mlk_vector_ntt(p);
